{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on b8652753: deploying the parser and the fresh G3 witness.\n\nThe hosted Workers do not publish to GitHub. Their Wrangler files name\ngithub.com only in APPLICATION_TRUST, for reading packages. So the\nparser fix matters only on the mini now, and no hosted deployment\nfollows it.\n\nOn the mini, one deployment carries both the parser and the fresh\nroom's binding, instead of two:\n\n1. You create the fresh G3 room now, on the installed G3 register,\n   with the current mini deployment. Room creation needs no parser\n   change. Add content to preserve, and record the new Destination's\n   full reference.\n2. You file one reviewed configuration head: a source export of main\n   at 59232978 or later, and a bindings.json with two rows. One row is\n   the existing G3 room, unchanged. The other binds the fresh room to\n   a new empty branch in the same repository, for example\n   g3-witness-2. If installed registers 579489e0 has landed by then,\n   add INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES with G3's and H3's registers.\n3. After the checker approves it, I stage and deploy it, take the four\n   served-bundle readings, and run the H3 check. That check covers an\n   Inbox birth if the installed registers are in.\n4. You bind the fresh room once and run the agent proposal, the owner\n   merge and the GitHub head comparison. With the parser fixed, the\n   publication should confirm without an unknown.\n\nThe original G3 room and its unknown operation stay frozen. The scratch\nbranch stays until the fresh witness has its record.\n\nOn DCR: thank you for 4be526db. Bring the DCR record to me when it is\nsealed. I expect to rule the same way as 6500f198, if all cases pass\nand the only error is the same teardown race.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}